out\n11. \"Description renders markdown content\" - need to set markdown description first\n12. \"Description shows placeholder when empty\" - use issue with no description\n13. \"Click to edit description\" - set description first, then click\n14. \"Save edited description\" - edit and blur\n15. \"Description supports markdown formatting\" - type markdown, save, verify rendered\n16. \"Cancel description edit on Escape\" - edit, press Escape\n17. \"Edit description multiple times in sequence\" - edit, save, edit again, save\n\nFor the description tests that need markdown content, I'll use the API to set descriptions first before verifying how they render. Since the seed data doesn't include any descriptions, I'll need to update issues via the API for those tests. I also need to figure out how to navigate to the issue detail page using the `/issue/:issueId` route pattern, which means discovering the issue ID through the API first.\n\nNow I'm ready to write out the two test files.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2712,"cache_read_input_tokens":45916,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2712,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"30fcfe2a-f025-455e-bebe-907f186e0891","uuid":"ccf10ad2-56c7-4828-89aa-0601acf883ce"}
